> I'm writing some code that uses geotiffio.h, and it's been working fine with a tiff file I have. Now, suddenly, I can't get the tie points:
> ```
>     double *tiePoints = nullptr;
>     double *pixelScale = nullptr;
>     uint16_t countTiePoints = 0, countPixelScale = 0;
> 
>     TIFFGetField(tiff, TIFFTAG_GEOTIEPOINTS, &countTiePoints, &tiePoints);
>     TIFFGetField(tiff, TIFFTAG_GEOPIXELSCALE, &countPixelScale, &pixelScale);
>     cout << countTiePoints << ", " << countPixelScale << endl;
> ```
> Gives me:
> 0, 3
> and my error message (I wrote): "No usable geotransform in GeoTIFF".
